# WeTravel Complete Database Schema Specification

This document defines the unified database schema for **WeTravel**, derived directly from the system architecture specification (`doc.text`).

The database is built on **PostgreSQL 16+** with the **`pgvector`** extension. Relational operations and transactional constraints are managed by the Node.js Orchestrator via **Prisma ORM**, while vector embeddings (`VECTOR(384)`) and semantic operations are managed by the FastAPI AI Engine via **SQLAlchemy** and `pgvector-python`.

---

## 1. PostgreSQL Extensions & Custom Types

```sql
-- Enable vector extension for vector embeddings
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;

-- Custom Enum Types
CREATE TYPE "Role" AS ENUM ('creator', 'admin', 'member');
CREATE TYPE "FriendshipStatus" AS ENUM ('pending', 'accepted', 'blocked');
CREATE TYPE "TripStatus" AS ENUM ('planning', 'ongoing', 'completed', 'archived');
CREATE TYPE "MessageType" AS ENUM ('text', 'image', 'receipt_upload', 'poll', 'ai_system');
CREATE TYPE "PollStatus" AS ENUM ('open', 'closed');
CREATE TYPE "ExpenseSource" AS ENUM ('manual_entry', 'ai_screenshot_ocr');
CREATE TYPE "ExpenseStatus" AS ENUM ('pending_approval', 'approved', 'rejected');
CREATE TYPE "SettlementStatus" AS ENUM ('pending', 'completed');
```

